  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "6f1c2a8e-4b1d-4c55-9a7e-1f3e0c2b9d10",
    "name": "NexusCommerce API",
    "description": "REST API for the General Store MVP backend (`ecom-server`, Spring Boot 3.5).\n\n## Quick start\n1. Start the stack: `docker compose up --build` in `ecom-server/` (API on `http://localhost:8080`).\n2. Import this collection and `NexusCommerce.local.postman_environment.json`, then select the **NexusCommerce – Local** environment.\n3. Run **Auth → Register customer**, then **Auth → Login as customer**. The login test script stores the JWT in `customerToken`.\n4. The create requests store their ids (`categoryId`, `productId`, `addressId`, `orderId`) automatically, so the folders can be run top to bottom.\n\n## Roles\nPublic registration always creates `ROLE_CUSTOMER`. There is no API for creating merchants or admins. To get one, register a normal user, then promote it in the database:\n\n```sql\nUPDATE users SET role = 'ROLE_MERCHANT' WHERE email = 'merchant@example.com';\nUPDATE users SET role = 'ROLE_ADMIN'    WHERE email = 'admin@example.com';\n```\n\nWith Docker: `docker compose exec db psql -U postgres -d nexus_commerce -c \"<sql>\"`. The change takes effect on the next request, because the role is read from the database each time.\n\n| Role | Can call |\n|---|---|\n| Public | auth, product and category reads, health |\n| CUSTOMER | cart, addresses, checkout, own orders |\n| MERCHANT | create, update and delete own products, list own products, catalog import |\n| ADMIN | create categories, catalog import, mark orders paid, replay Stripe webhook events |\n\n## Response envelope\nEvery response uses the same shape:\n```json\n{ \"success\": true, \"message\": \"...\", \"data\": { }, \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-24T10:00:00Z\" }\n```\nOn errors, `success` is `false` and `data` may hold field-level validation details. List endpoints return a Spring `Page` in `data` (`content`, `totalElements`, `totalPages`, `number`, `size`) and accept `page`, `size` and `sort` query parameters.\n\n## Products and variants (FR-IM-02)\nA **parent product** is the catalog record: code, name, brand, descriptions and category. Each purchasable **variant** is its own SKU with its own price, stock, images and attributes (variant name, colour, size, material, pattern, style). Cart and checkout work with variant ids. `/api/products/{id}` returns one variant together with its `parent` and a `variants` list for the variant selector. A product without variants is a parent with one SKU; its parent code defaults to the SKU.\n\n## Catalog import (FR-IM-01)\n`POST /api/catalog/import` loads a CSV or Excel (.xlsx) file in the template format. Download the template from **Catalog Import → Download template**. `postman/catalog-import-sample.csv` is a ready-made example.\n\n- Mandatory per row: `Product_Name`, `Category` (an existing category's slug or name), `Product_Status` (`DRAFT`, `ACTIVE`, `INACTIVE` or `ARCHIVED`), `Selling_Price`, `Inventory_Qty`, and at least one of `Image_1_URL` … `Image_5_URL`.\n- Rows sharing a `Parent_Product_ID` become variants of one parent and must share a category.\n- Leave `SKU_ID` and `Parent_Product_ID` blank to have them generated: parents as `GS-<CATEGORY>-<SUBCATEGORY>-<SEQUENCE>` (e.g. `GS-CL-MEN-001`), variants as `<parent>-<COLOR>-<SIZE>` (e.g. `GS-CL-MEN-001-BLK-M`). Rows are grouped into one parent by `Category`, `Subcategory`, `Brand` and `Product_Name` without its trailing variant part (`Tee — Black, M` groups as `Tee`). Re-importing the sheet joins the existing parents and rejects variants that already exist. The report's `imported` list gives each row's SKU and parent code.\n- A bad row is rejected on its own; the valid rows still import. The report lists each rejected row's number, SKU and reason.\n- A SKU that repeats within the file, or already exists in the catalog, is rejected. Re-import as an update (FR-IM-09) is not built yet.\n- Other template columns (MRP, Tax_Code, SEO fields and so on) are accepted but not stored yet, and are listed in `ignoredColumns`.\n- Limits: 10 MB per file and 5,000 data rows (`CATALOG_IMPORT_MAX_FILE_SIZE`, `CATALOG_IMPORT_MAX_ROWS`).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
