    {
      "name": "Catalog Import",
      "description": "Bulk catalog import (FR-IM-01/02). Requires `ROLE_MERCHANT` or `ROLE_ADMIN`; uses `merchantToken`. Imported products are owned by the caller. See the collection description for the column rules.",
      "auth": {
        "type": "bearer",
        "bearer": [
          {
            "key": "token",
            "value": "{{merchantToken}}",
            "type": "string"
          }
        ]
      },
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Download template",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('CSV attachment', () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Content-Disposition')).to.include('catalog-import-template.csv'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/catalog/import/template",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "catalog",
                "import",
                "template"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Downloads `catalog-import-template.csv`: every column the importer reads, plus two example rows (one parent with two variants). Use **Send and Download** to save it. The response is raw CSV, not the ApiResponse envelope."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Import catalog file",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const report = pm.response.json().data;",
                  "pm.test('Report totals add up', () => pm.expect(report.importedRows + report.failedRows).to.eql(report.totalRows));",
                  "console.log('Import report', report);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "file",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": "catalog-import-sample.csv",
                  "description": "A .csv (UTF-8) or .xlsx file. Only the first sheet of a workbook is read."
                }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/catalog/import",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "catalog",
                "import"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Uploads a template file as `multipart/form-data`, in a part named `file`. Re-select the file after importing the collection: Postman stores only its name. The sample is `postman/catalog-import-sample.csv`. Its rows use category slug `clothing`, so create that category first (or edit the file). Row 5 fails on purpose to show the error report.\n\nReturns `200` with a report even when some rows are rejected:\n\n| Field | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| totalRows | data rows read (blank rows skipped) |\n| importedRows / failedRows | rows written / rejected |\n| parentProductsCreated | new parent products |\n| ignoredColumns | columns in the file the importer doesn't read yet |\n| errors[] | `row` (as numbered in the file, header = 1), `sku`, `reason` (all problems, joined with `; `) |\n\nErrors for the whole file: `400` wrong file type, unreadable file, missing required columns, no data rows or too many rows; `400` no `file` part; `403` not a merchant or admin; `413` file too large; `409` another request inserted the same SKU mid-import (nothing is written)."
          },
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "200 Partial import",
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "POST",
                "header": [],
                "url": {
                  "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/catalog/import",
                  "host": [
                    "{{baseUrl}}"
                  ],
                  "path": [
                    "api",
                    "catalog",
                    "import"
                  ]
                }
              },
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
              "header": [
                {
                  "key": "Content-Type",
                  "value": "application/json"
                }
              ],
              "body": "{\n  \"success\": true,\n  \"message\": \"Imported 3 of 4 rows\",\n  \"data\": {\n    \"fileName\": \"catalog-import-sample.csv\",\n    \"totalRows\": 4,\n    \"importedRows\": 3,\n    \"failedRows\": 1,\n    \"parentProductsCreated\": 2,\n    \"ignoredColumns\": [],\n    \"errors\": [\n      {\n        \"row\": 5,\n        \"sku\": \"GS-CL-MEN-003\",\n        \"reason\": \"Unknown category 'no-such-category'; Selling_Price is required\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-24T10:00:00Z\"\n}"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
